Figure 2: Derivation of a physically motivated compactness threshold from the one-dimensional relations between
$\log_{10}(\Sigma_{1.5}/(\rm{M}_{\odot}\,\mathrm{kpc}^{-1.5}))$ and different galaxy-evolution tracers:
(a) luminosity-weighted mean stellar age;
(b) stellar metallicity;
(c) stellar [Mg/Fe];
(d) specific star formation rate;
(e) stellar velocity dispersion; and
(f) ex-situ stellar mass fraction.
For each tracer, the left subpanel shows all individual galaxies (grey points) overlaid on a kernel density estimate (KDE), with the median relation shown in black and the 16th–84th percentile range in grey. The right subpanel shows the smoothed median together with its derivative (red; right axis); the dashed vertical line marks the high-compactness maximum of the derivative adopted as the compactness threshold.
